# Astro DAG bundle sync: changes under dags/ (or this file) on merge trigger the
# Woodpecker DAG deploys — development → Astro "dev", forno → Astro "forno",
# master/hotfix → Astro "prod".
# (ci-astro steps use /bin/sh — keep scripts POSIX; no bash pipefail.)
#
# Syntax: every consumer of this file sets AIRFLOW__CORE__DAG_IGNORE_FILE_SYNTAX=glob
# — the data_ai dev/forno/prod deployments (infrastructure
# cloud/apps/astronomer/data_ai_platform/*/main.tf) and the local `astro/` project
# (astro/Dockerfile). So the glob patterns below are the ones that take effect. The
# luigijr / yellowbrick deployments do run Airflow's default regexp syntax, but they
# never receive this file: their bags are staged from dags/luigijr only.
cross/base/
**/spark_jobs/
**/tools/
**/validation/
# NOTE: deliberately NO `*_validation_dag.py` pattern here. Split validation twin
# DAGs must stay active on prod — during the Astro cutover they arrive as per-DAG
# stubs from the legacy `make create-dag-files` chain, and afterwards as prod-only
# `_validation_bundle_*.py` bundles. Since every consumer is on glob syntax, adding
# that pattern back would silently stop those DQ validation DAGs on prod. Local
# Airflow parses the stubs too (they are gitignored generated files — `rm` them if
# you want a lighter local bag); forno/dev never receive any.
# Standalone emr-migration twin/emr/compare DAGs — where the pipeline generates
# bundles they are parsed via _astro_bundles/platform_migration/_*_bundle_*.py
# (exec-passthrough) instead of the ~714 individual files; on the legacy chain they
# are intentionally not parsed at all (on-demand EMR validation twins). Files still
# ship in the rsync payload for bundle exec and worker re-import; only the processor
# skips the individual paths.
platform/migration_twin_*/
platform/migration_emr_*/
platform/migration_compare_*/
platform/migration_assets/
# Defensive regexp equivalent: matches the same migration folders if a deployment
# ever loses DAG_IGNORE_FILE_SYNTAX=glob. Inert under glob (parens are literal), so
# it is safe to keep alongside the globs.
platform/migration_(twin|emr|compare)_
